{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_fastify_fastifybackend", "label": "FastifyBackend", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The default backend and the production recommendation - the most battle-tested Node HTTP framework, with the framework's own actor-routing overhead as the next bottleneck for hot routes.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/fastify.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_fastify_bodylimit", "label": "bodyLimit", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The one Fastify setting the framework fills in: left unset it is 1 MiB, the same cap the Express and Hono backends apply, so which requests are accepted does not change with the backend. Passing your own still wins.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/fastify.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_fastify_hard_dependency", "label": "Fastify as a hard dependency", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Fastify installs with the framework so the default backend needs nothing extra; Express and Hono are optional peer dependencies installed on demand.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/fastify.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_fastify_raw_fastify_instance", "label": "Raw Fastify instance escape hatch", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "withPlugin and backend.fastify expose plugins the DSL does not - JWT/OAuth, schema validation, CORS, compression. The DSL owns routing, Fastify plugins own cross-cutting concerns. Register route-touching plugins before binding, or they conflict with the framework's registrations.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/fastify.mdx", "sou